    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="97d0f84e-8aa4-5f5c-9251-ae0aa5e965ae" activityNameId="3d2d10b4-533f-5673-8a74-4483a101261c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Expanded clay, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Expanded clay, at plant
Expanded at 1’200 °C in a rotary furnace. Heavy fuel oil is used for heating. Bulk density of expanded clay: 260 - 500kg/m3;
UUID: 4b8a04c6-3015-3f7c-aec0-7ba1b193e3f8
includes the raw materials, the transport to the finishing plant and some internal transports, the energy carrier, some packaging materials, the infrastructure and the emissions
Location: For some exchanges CH, RER and GLO modules have been used as proxy.
Technology: The mined clay is mixed with water, ground, sometimes granulated and burned at reverse flow in a rotary furnace at 1’200 °C. The included organic materials burn and the clay pellets expand with the help of heavy fuel oil. The surface melts and produces a sintered shell.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: See geography
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4b8a04c6-3015-3f7c-aec0-7ba1b193e3f8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="948c6fdb-25b0-54ae-bf5c-e320176f724c" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
